And so when we imagine what they're going to be like in the future, the first thing that pops in our head is, they're going to become conscious. Yeah, I think there's a lot of projection happening there. I also think that before we get to the question of robot rights and consciousness, we have to ask ourselves, how do robots fit into our lives when we perceive them as conscious, because I think that's when it starts to get morally messy and not when they actually inherently have some sort of consciousness. If humans have a tendency to anthropomorphize machines to see them as human. It isn't surprising that
所以当我们想象它们未来会是什么样子时，我们脑海中浮现的第一件事就是：它们将变得有意识。是的，我认为那里发生了很多投射。我也认为，在我们探讨机器人权利和意识的问题之前，当我们把机器人视为有意识的时，我们必须问自己：机器人是如何融入我们的生活的？因为我认为正是从那时起，事情开始变得在道德上陷入泥潭，而不是当它们本身真正具备某种意识时。如果人类有将机器拟人化、将它们视为人的倾向，那么

